Rotary Wing Aerodynamics
AE 667
Dhwanil Shukla


The course will...
o Teach you a ton about rotors
o Force you to do open-ended assignments
o Give you some programming practice
o Probably make you better engineers overall (no promises!)


Course Outline
1. Introduction
2. Rotor Hover Performance Prediction Methods
3. Vertical Descent of Rotors
4. Rotors in Forward Flight
5. Vehicle Performance
6. Advanced Topics


Learning Outcomes
By the end of the course, we should be able to:
1. Analyse & design rotors/propellers for performance in hover/climb using
Momentum theory and Blade Element Momentum theory
2. Predict basic helicopter blade and rotor dynamics in a steady level
forward flight
3. Find pilot inputs necessary to achieve trim conditions in a steady level
forward flight
4. Estimate helicopter performance based on design parameters
5. Follow current research in the field of rotary wing aerodynamics


